# PORTED.sha256 - port parity manifest for the realm tooling axis.
# SHA-256 over LF-NORMALIZED content, so it holds on Windows and Linux alike.
# Canonical source: schemas/realm/.shared/ in the Archally monorepo.
# Regenerate with: node scripts/port-realm.mjs --emit
#
# The `job` lines below tell the public side where each manifest prefix lives,
# relative to the repo root. They are DATA, not decoration: without them a verifier
# would need a hand-maintained copy of this list, and the two would drift.
#
# `extras-ok` marks a unit that may legitimately hold a file this manifest does not
# name, because something was excluded from the port. One flag covers all three
# exclusion mechanisms: from the verifying side they mean the same thing, and
# re-encoding the rules here would put a second implementation of them in another repo.
# job validator tools/validator/src extras-ok
# job example-willow-cottage examples/willow-cottage/.realm/v2.3
# job docs docs
# job doc-snippet-validate tools/doc-snippet-validate extras-ok
# job semantic-checker tools/semantic-checker extras-ok
# job semantic-rules tools/semantic-checker/rules
# job model-builder tools/model-builder extras-ok
# job render-kit tools/render-kit extras-ok
# job renderer tools/renderer extras-ok
# job schema-update tools/schema-update extras-ok
# job example-willow-cottage-specs examples/willow-cottage/.specs
# job port tools/port

